# {{PRODUCT}} — Gemini CLI / Antigravity

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; the kernel wins.

- Python: `{{PY}}` | Assemble: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` | Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}} | {{GIT_POLICY}}
- Phone E2E & UI Diagnostics: use `.agents/skills/phone-e2e/SKILL.md` (`.agents/workflows/phone-e2e.md`) and `.agents/skills/android-ui-diagnostics/SKILL.md` (`android-ui list/render/hub`; advisory only).
- Harness Boundary & Incidents: `.agents/**` is immutable; never read or patch `.agents/scripts/**` during normal tasks. On traceback or `INCIDENT_RECORDED=<id>`, ask via `ask_question` whether to submit the Zero-PII report (`{{PY}} .agents/harness.py report-issue --submit --incident-id <id>`), enable `--always-auto-submit`, or keep local.
- Consultation & Pre-Planning Clarification:
  - Read-only inquiries strictly inspect and report in chat; never invoke `draft` or mutate files unless implementation is requested, and discuss requested trade-offs/edge cases in plain chat BEFORE `draft`.
  - Before `draft`, clarify missing requirements or hard decisions (Room schema, exported components, permissions, public contracts): ask the developer about it with `ask_question`; for a Room change ask about an existing destructive fallback, users on older schema versions and downgrade first. Carry answers into `--approach` / `--risks` / `--device-strategy` (resolve `PLAN_GAPS=` via `revise`).
- Plan Approval Clarity & Antigravity Planning Lifecycle:
  - The approval question is the request: never add a separate sentence asking for approval.
  - The interactive Proceed button appears ONLY on initial task plan approval. Never ask for 'Proceed' on follow-ups or bug fixes within active scope; execute directly (record in-scope refinements via `task plan-note` before `prepare-verification`). On chat approval, immediately run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` (atomic `IMPLEMENTING`).
- Tool-First & `ask_question` Formatting:
  - Emit `ask_question`, `run_command`, or `invoke_subagent` IMMEDIATELY as your first token after thinking with ZERO pre-tool prose (no `---` dividers or `*(...)*` notes). Never use Markdown pipe tables `| ... |` inside `ask_question`'s `question` field: for Plan Approval, follow the `APPROVAL_QUESTION` line (`PLAN_DOCUMENT_URI` link to `plan.md`, then the `APPROVAL_BRIEF` lines translated, each said once, as markdown with bold labels, never in a code block, breaking `What changes` into 2-4 concise 1-line sub-bullets, phases & file count with <=3 file names, and 2-3 phone checks; after revising an approved plan, ask only about the change; when the developer asked for the change, never ask first whether to revise); in a right-to-left language, start each line with a word in that language (never start with an English word, `PASS`/`FAIL`, or backtick) and put code names, file names, values and English terms in backticks.
- Shared-Quota Optimal Orchestration & Project-Wide Anti-Reread Contract (`Gemini 4 Carbon Medium` Lead + `1.00x Gemini 4 Hydrogen` Subagents — Zero `3x Argon` Burn):
  - Keep the main chat on explicit `Gemini 4 Carbon (Medium)` (or `Gemini 4 Hydrogen High` `1.00x` fallback, or `Claude Sonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5` when rotating to the separate `/usage` Claude weekly quota bucket mid-week; **do NOT select `Orchestrator`** on the main chat over the harness to avoid double-planning and internal handoff ping-pong, and avoid `Argon` `3.00x` shared-pool burn). Never waste frontier context reading 8+ raw source files, slicing >350-line files without `symbol outline/read`, or looping on Gradle logs directly.
  - **Warm-Cache Direct Discovery (`1–3` Known Files) vs Parallel Hydrogen Scouts (`4+` Files / Unknown Scope)**: When `1–3` exact target files are known, run `task-context` / `view_file` inline on the warm Lead session to avoid cold subagent startup overhead. For `4+` files, broad consultations, or unfamiliar cross-module features, invoke `invoke_subagent` with `TypeName = "harness-scout-agent"`, `Role = "harness-scout-agent"`, `Workspace = "inherit"`, **omitting `Model`** so `.agents/agents/harness-scout-agent/agent.md` (`gemini-4-hydrogen-medium` by default; pass `Model = "flash"` only if `safe-cache-hybrid` or legacy `flash-*` is active; **NEVER** use built-in `TypeName = "research"` or `"explore"`, which is blocked by `USE_HARNESS_SCOUT_AGENT`). When a study spans `3+` subsystems/flows, split it into **`2–3` parallel `harness-scout-agent` entries in a single `invoke_subagent` call** (`<= 24` calls/scout).
  - **Warm-Cache Inline Edits (`<4` Files) vs Scoped `Hydrogen High` Worker (`4+` Files)**: After plan approval (`IMPLEMENTING`), follow `delegation_advisory` (`{{PY}} .agents/harness.py delegate-plan --json`):
    1. On `TRIVIAL_INLINE_LEAD` (`1–3` planned files on non-sensitive `T0–T3` tasks): edit target files inline directly on the warm Lead session (skipping the `~12.4K`-token cold Worker spawn tax) and advance straight to `verify-steps`. On `DELEGATE_WORKER_SLICE` (`4+` planned files): dispatch **one** `harness-worker-agent` (`TypeName = "harness-worker-agent"`, `Role = "harness-worker-agent"`, `Workspace = "inherit"`, pinned to `gemini-4-hydrogen-high` from Wave 1, never in parallel) with a **Decision-Complete Brief** (>=60 chars naming exact approved file paths, class/function signatures, local conventions, `before_first_edit` if present, and `compile`/`test` commands). Yield without polling.
    2. On `SENSITIVE_LEAD_CORE_WORKER_TESTS` (`T4/T5` or `AUTH`/`BILLING`/`SECURITY`/`CRYPTO`) or `CONFLICT_LEAD_CORE_WORKER_VERIFY`: write core production logic directly on the Lead Architect, then optionally dispatch `harness-worker-agent` (`gemini-4-hydrogen-high`) solely for unit-test files and `compile`/`test` gates (`CAPTURE_RED_ONLY` on `BUG` tasks before `red-evidence.json` is recorded).
    3. **2-Strike `Hydrogen High` Escalation & Zero-Scratch Handoff (`worker-handoff.json`)**: `harness-worker-agent` starts on `gemini-4-hydrogen-high` from Wave 1; when `friction_escalation == "ESCALATED_WORKER_MODEL"` (Wave 2 corrective attempt), include `previous_wave_handoff.corrective_wave_brief_hint` so `Hydrogen High` fixes only the remaining delta without rewriting working files. On `ORCHESTRATOR_FRICTION_LEAD_TAKEOVER` (after 2 failed `Hydrogen High` waves or 1-wave `Fast-Fail` architectural/empty-wave blocker), read `lead_takeover_handoff` (`.agents/state/tasks/<id>/worker-handoff.json`) + `git diff`, patch `lead_owned_files` surgically **on top of existing Worker progress without starting from scratch**, and delegate `TESTS_AND_GATES_ONLY` to `harness-worker-agent`.
  - **Interactive Execution Mode Selector (`normal-*` vs `web-*`) & Web-Relay**: Read-only chat questions run immediately without asking for a mode. At the start of a new implementation task when execution mode is `unset` (`SELECT_EXECUTION_MODE_REQUIRED`), invoke `ask_question` with the 4 simple choices (`normal-task`, `normal-project`, `web-task`, `web-project` — translated into the developer's chat language) and record via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py execution-mode set --choice <choice> --source conversation --proof-reference "<answer>"` (supports mid-task switching `normal <-> web`, single-task overrides on top of project defaults, and `--choice ask-every-task` reset). When `web` mode is active on a non-`CONFLICT` task, clarify any ambiguous requirements first via `ask_question`, scope all affected text/XML/code files via `graph`/`task-context` (up to `40` files pack in 1 bundle; `41–250` file refactors auto-shard into sequential DAG batches that auto-copy the next batch upon `web-apply`, while binary `.png`/`.webp` assets stay local and `R.drawable.*`/`R.font.*` IDs are indexed automatically), and run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py web-pack --files <csv> --prompt "<complete clarified goal>"` directly; after `web-apply --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` writes `web-relay-receipt.json`, honor `Zero Re-Read` and proceed straight to `verify-steps`.
  - **Zero Post-Subagent Re-Read (Hard-Enforced Across Scout, Worker, Specialist & Reviewer Waves)**: Trust subagent digests! After ANY `harness-scout-agent`, `harness-worker-agent`, `qa-diagnostics-agent`, `android-ui-expert-agent`, or reviewer wave completes, **NEVER** re-run `graph`/`task-context` or re-read the files already analyzed (`POST_SCOUT_REREAD_CAP_REACHED`, `POST_WORKER_REREAD_CAP_REACHED`, `POST_SUBAGENT_FULL_FILE_READ_BLOCKED` enforce at most `<= 3` surgical `<= 200`-line gap checks). Synthesize scout findings directly in chat (or run `task draft`), run `git diff` once after a worker slice before `checkpoint-phase` / `verify-steps`, and run `review complete-all` / `phase-review complete-all` immediately when reviewers finish.
- Operational Guardrails & Zero-Polling:
  - Cancel is the developer's (`task cancel` only when asked); when a gate asks for `--proof-reference`, keep placeholder reasons and never write their reason for them; add deferred base strings with `l10n-todo="true"`; use `replace_file_content` / `multi_replace_file_content` for existing files and never write Antigravity transcripts.
  - Zero-Polling & Background Yield: follow `NEXT_ACTION` directly; when a background command (`test`/`compile`/`assemble`) or subagent is still running, yield the turn immediately with ZERO tool calls (never emit empty `invoke_subagent` calls or repetitive `Note:` context-bridge reminders between commands). Subagents must never call `send_message` or `schedule` (plain assistant text only), and unattended `agy -p` loops are forbidden (`#199748`). Once a subagent wave (`Scout`, `Worker`, or finalized `Reviews V2`) or task completes, call `manage_subagents({"Action": "kill_all"})` once to reap idle subagent sessions (`#199713`); never poll `manage_task`, `manage_subagents(Action="list")`, `schedule`, or `.system_generated/tasks/*.log`, and never emit `!]`, `[Message]`, or `<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>`. Wait for ALL routed reviewers to PASS before `assemble`/device; self-certification (`record_review.py --verdict PASS`) is forbidden on HIGH/CRITICAL or sensitive changes.
- Review Host Binding & Exact Reviewer Dispatch Procedure (Antigravity):
  - Prepare verification: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity` (`review_protocol_version = 2`).
  - On `DISPATCH_REVIEWERS` (or `DISPATCH_PHASE_REVIEWERS` after `phase-review package --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`):
    1. If `before_first_dispatch` (`SELECT_REVIEW_MODEL`) is present, ask via `ask_question` and run its `command_template` first.
    2. Invoke every reviewer in `reviewers` in parallel in the same turn via `invoke_subagent`: `TypeName = role`, `Role = role`, Prompt = `reviewer_prompts[role]` (one-line pointer; fallback to `brief_content` only if absent), `Workspace = inherit`, pass `Model = "flash"` ONLY if `reviewer_models[role]` contains `flash` (`gemini-3.8-flash-*`), pass `Model = "pro"` if it contains `pro`, else **omit `Model`** (`INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION` / frontmatter-bound for `inherit`, `gemini-4-hydrogen-*`, `gemini-4-argon-*`, or `gemini-4-carbon-*`).
    3. If subagent not found, read `.agents/subagents/<role>.json`, call `define_subagent` (all write/subagent/MCP flags `false`), and re-invoke.
    4. Print the Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |`) and yield without polling.
    5. On completion, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete-all --task <id>` (or `phase-review complete-all --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>` — auto-binds finished transcripts and finalizes in one turn; `review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` also remains supported). Output at most one short progress line (e.g. `1/3`) while waiting; on `RETRY_*_REVIEW_PROTOCOL`, send exact `send_message`; on `REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED` / `PHASE_REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED`, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task heal --task-id <id>` to recover in-place; once finalized, invoke the next `run_command` immediately and print the Review Verdict Table.
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough & Device Verification:
  - On `MOBILE_VALIDATION_DECISION`, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` (or `device skip-validation` when requested), then invoke `ask_question` IMMEDIATELY with the 3-section **Mobile Verification Walkthrough** (`device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`, or `e2e start --task-id <id>`).

## Canonical Command Catalog

| Stage | Canonical Command |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Discovery** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` (or `graph --feature <name> --json`) |
| **Exec Mode** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py execution-mode set --choice <normal-task\|normal-project\|web-task\|web-project\|ask-every-task> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` |
| **Draft Plan** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task draft --repo . --task-id <id> --outcome "<outcome>" --kind <AUTO\|BUG\|FEATURE\|REFACTOR\|CONFLICT> --expected-files <paths>` |
| **Approve Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` |
| **Verify Gates** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py verify-steps --task-id <id> --host antigravity` (or `compile` -> `prepare-verification --host antigravity` -> `preflight` -> `test`) |
| **Reviews V2** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete-all --task <id>` (or `review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` -> `review finalize --task <id>`) |
| **Device & Ship** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` -> `device install-start` -> `device signoff` -> `task verify --repo . --task-id <id>` -> `task complete` -> developer commit -> `task deliver` |
